{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"06ea1b172c33a96f","name":"card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/WorldAtWar/units/card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"60th CAVALRY REGIMENT","text":"Players can only give one order each turn.","flavorText":"The 60th Cavalry Regiment was a military unit of the 3rd Cavalry Division of the Red Army of the Soviet Union. The division was first formed in 1923 and participated in the invasion of Poland in 1939, but at the start of Operation Barbarossa in 1941 it defended against the Axis invaders as part of the 5th Cavalry Corps of the 6th Army of the Southwestern Front. That same year the division was redesignated to 5th Guards Cavalry Division for its skillful combat performance against the Axis forces. From 1944 to 1945 the division served under the 1st and 2nd Baltic Front, but was moved to 3rd Belorussian Front where it served until the end of the war. ","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment_title","SourceString":"60th CAVALRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"60th CAVALRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment_text","SourceString":"Players can only give one order each turn.","LocalizedString":"Players can only give one order each turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_60th_cavalry_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 60th Cavalry Regiment was a military unit of the 3rd Cavalry Division of the Red Army of the Soviet Union. The division was first formed in 1923 and participated in the invasion of Poland in 1939, but at the start of Operation Barbarossa in 1941 